    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Abstract\r\nThis report examines the implementation and effectiveness of community schools in California, New York, Maryland, and Florida, with a particular focus on strategic education governance and the role of community engagement in improving educational outcomes. The study utilizes the OECD Strategic Education Governance (SEG) framework, which emphasizes six domains: accountability, capacity, knowledge governance, stakeholder involvement, strategic thinking, and a whole-of-system perspective. Through literature reviews, interviews with community school leaders, and analysis of best practices, this report provides recommendations to enhance California's community school initiatives.\r\n\r\nCalifornia's Community Schools Partnership Program (CCSPP) aims to transform schools into community hubs that address the holistic needs of students by integrating health, social services, and academic support. The program is funded through a significant state investment of $4.1 billion, allocated until 2028. The study identifies key challenges in California's current implementation, such as inconsistent accountability, fragmented governance, and limited stakeholder engagement.\r\n\r\nDrawing on successful practices from New York, Maryland, and Florida, the report recommends adopting coordinated policy frameworks, integrated support systems, regional collaboration networks, and robust data-sharing mechanisms. These strategies are intended to improve accountability, capacity building, and strategic planning in California's community schools.\r\n\r\nUltimately, this report underscores the importance of a cohesive and collaborative approach to community schooling, emphasizing the need for comprehensive support systems that engage multiple stakeholders and address the diverse needs of students and their communities.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
